Description: Validates text and converts it between the Unicode
    Transformation Formats UTF-8, UTF-16 and UTF-32, in either byte order,
    and Latin-1, counts characters, detects encodings, and encodes and
    decodes Base64, with a bundled copy of the
    'simdutf' library (<https://github.com/simdutf/simdutf>). 'simdutf'
    chooses single instruction, multiple data (SIMD) code for the running
    processor at first use, so validation and conversion run at gigabytes
    per second; its methods are described by Keiser and Lemire (2021)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2010.03090>, Lemire and Mula (2022)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2109.10433> and Mula and Lemire (2020)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1910.05109>. Every validation and conversion can
    report the position of the first ill-formed sequence, in the units of
    the input. Character, raw and list-of-raw input are accepted, and
    invalid input can raise an error, be replaced with U+FFFD, or give a
    missing value. The same functions are published to other packages as a
    registered C interface.
